        "abstract": "Principles of dynamic programming and its application to discrete-utterance and connected-speech recognition are introduced and discussed. The deterministic form, used for template matching for connected speech, is described in detail, and a number of algorithms are examined. The Viterbi algorithm, which is a form of dynamic programming for a stochastic system, is briefly discussed.<<ETX xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">&gt;</ETX>",
